          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is A Water Fountain For Cats Good To Cats?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, a water fountain for cats can be beneficial to cats. </p><p>Cats are more inclined to drink from flowing water because it mimics natural water sources like streams. The continuous circulation of water in fountains also keeps it fresh and oxygenated, encouraging your cat to drink more, which promotes better hydration and overall health. </p><p>Proper hydration can help prevent urinary tract issues and kidney problems in cats.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_eHJy4J": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What Features Should I Look for In Safe Cat Water Fountain?",
            "text": "<p>Such as BPA-free materials, a quiet motor, an easy-to-clean design, and an effective filtration system. Filters that remove impurities like pet hair, food particles, and debris ensure that your cat has fresh, clean water at all times.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_FCKyUi": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I Use Tap Water In My Dog Water Fountain?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, you can use tap water in a dog water fountain, but it's advisable to use filtered or purified water if possible to reduce mineral deposits and impurities. If you're using tap water, ensure the fountain has a reliable filter to keep the water clean and safe for your dog. Regular cleaning is also essential to prevent build-up from minerals or bacteria.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_hXRenD": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How Do I Choose The Safe Dog Water Fountain?",
            "text": "<p>When choosing a safe dog water fountain for your dog, prioritize non-toxic materials. Ensure ease of cleaning, and consider features like filters, and quiet operation. These factors will help you pick a dispenser that provides your pet with fresh, clean water.</p><p>The Oneisall Dog Water Fountain uses 304SUS food-grade stainless steel, which is safer and healthier than plastic. It can be equipped with a filter and operates quietly, with noise levels below 35 decibels. </p><p>Only follow these four steps to clean the water pump:</p><ul><li>Gently break open the pump cover</li><li>Remove the pump cover, and open the impeller cover</li><li>Remove the impeller</li><li>Clean the parts with dish soap and warm water</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "question_MdwjM8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is The Pet Water Fountain Easy To Assemble?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Most pet water fountains are easy to assemble and designed to be user-friendly. The process usually involves a few simple steps and can be done in minutes. </p><p>Here's a basic outline of what to expect:</p><ul><li>Put filter cotton into the filter box</li><li>Assemble the pump</li><li>Fill the tank with water</li><li>Put on the cover drinking tray and insert the faucet</li></ul><p>Most pet water fountains come with an instruction manual that includes a step-by-step guide. Following this ensures that all parts are properly installed and the fountain functions correctly.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_N664PD": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When Should I Add Water To Pet Water Fountain?",
            "text": "<p>You should add water to your pet's water fountain when the water level gets low. </p><p>Here are some ways to help you determine when you need to add water:</p><ul><li>Water Level Indicator: The Oneisall pet water fountain has a water level indicator. When the water level is low, a red light will be displayed to issue a no-water warning.</li><li>Reduced Water Flow: If the water flow becomes weak or slow, it's a sign that the water level is too low and the pump may not be working efficiently.</li><li>Noise from the Pump: If the pump starts making louder than usual noise, it may be struggling due to low water levels and needs refilling.</li><li>Daily Check: You can see the remaining water level. It's a good habit to check the water level daily especially if you have multiple pets or if your pet drinks a lot.</li></ul><p>Keeping the water level topped up ensures the pet water fountain runs smoothly and helps prevent the pump from burning out.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_nq9TUn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does A Pet Drinking Fountain Need A Filter?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, a pet drinking fountain needs a filter.</p><p> Filters help remove impurities, hair, food particles, and other debris from the water, keeping it clean and safe for your pet. Many filters also have activated charcoal to help reduce odor and improve the taste of the water, which can encourage your pet to drink more. </p><p>It is recommended to purchase the set containing a filter. About four filters need to be replaced in a month. Be sure to regularly check and replace the filter as the manufacturer recommends.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_j68zTR": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I Use A Cat Water Fountain For Both Cats And Dogs?",
            "text": "<p>Yes, many cat water fountains are designed to accommodate both cats and dogs. Choose a cat water fountain for your pet's size and breed. Larger dogs may require a pet drinking fountain with a higher water capacity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_wkgHpN": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do Cat Water Fountains Require Electricity?",
            "text": "<p>Most cat water fountains need to plug into power the pump that circulates the water. Some cat water fountain models are USB-powered, while others use traditional outlets. Check the pet drinking fountain details for power requirements before purchasing.</p>"
